13ie|n|The hard, white, opaque, fine-grained substance constituting the tusks of the elephant. It is a variety of dentine, characterized by the minuteness and close arrangement of the tubes, as also by their double flexure. It is used in manufacturing articles of ornament or utility. ; The tusks themselves of the elephant, etc. ; Any carving executed in ivory. ; Teeth; as, to show one's ivories.	a:1w1v,1,3~1w1v,1,3
13ig|n|A plant of the genus Hedera (H. helix), common in Europe. Its leaves are evergreen, dark, smooth, shining, and mostly five-pointed; the flowers yellowish and small; the berries black or yellow. The stem clings to walls and trees by rootlike fibers.	N:25l6,14,5~25l6,14,5
